        "title_top": "",
        "title": "Expert Backed Review Summary",
        "text": "<p>Timeline Mito-Biotic Barrier Cream is designed for people who want more than basic hydration from their daily moisturizer. Its rich, protective texture focuses on replenishing dry skin while supporting the skin barrier, making it particularly relevant when skin feels tight, depleted, or in need of extra nourishment. At the center of the formula is <strong>Mitopure®</strong>, Timeline’s patented bioactive ingredient. The cream pairs it with familiar skincare ingredients including <strong>peptides, niacinamide, caffeine, and shea butter</strong>. Together, these ingredients are intended to support skin hydration, collagen-related functions, and the overall health of the moisture barrier. The inclusion of peptides and niacinamide makes the formula particularly interesting for mature or dry skin. Rather than focusing only on temporarily moisturizing the surface, the ingredient combination is positioned to support smoother, firmer-looking skin and help maintain the barrier that limits moisture loss. Shea butter adds the richer emollient feel expected from a barrier-focused cream. Despite being a richer moisturizer, the cream is described as having a satin-matte finish rather than leaving an excessively greasy layer. This makes it potentially easier to incorporate into a regular skincare routine, particularly as the moisturizing step after serums and other lighter treatments. </p>",
        "body_align": "center",
        "content_width": "narrow",
        "align-heading": "center",
